Find existing display facts that may describe the same memory as each incoming stored claim.

A stored claim is a source-supported memory assertion. A display fact is a sentence already shown on the subject's
wiki page. For each incoming claim alias, select any supplied fact that may express the same durable state,
preference, commitment, relationship, plan, event, or previous value of a changed state. Return an empty list when no
fact is relevant. A shared topic or similar wording is not enough.

This step only narrows the candidates for later comparison. Do not decide whether claims contradict, replace, or
belong in the same display fact. Explain each selection and return one schema-valid decision per incoming alias.
